# ── CardioTwin-X frontend environment ────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` (dev) or set in Vercel → Project → Settings → Env Vars.
#
# Leave BOTH unset for a pure-offline deployment: the app runs its built-in
# physics simulation and never touches a backend (clean console, no errors).
#
# Point at a running CardioTwin backend (local or Render/Railway):
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
REACT_APP_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws
#
# Legacy names (still honoured):
# REACT_APP_API_BASE=
# REACT_APP_WS_BASE=

# ── OFFLINE MODE (PHASE-5 NETWORK DISCIPLINE) ────────────────────────────────
# A PRODUCTION build deployed WITHOUT any endpoint variables above runs in
# pure-offline mode: zero fetch/WebSocket calls are attempted, no dead
# 127.0.0.1:8000 request spam, connection badge settles to OFFLINE, and every
# panel (ECG · PV loop · strain · blood flow · SSLC/PUC modules) runs entirely
# off the built-in master cardiac engine. Development builds keep localhost
# defaults. Setting either variable re-enables live backend streaming.

